# Engineering philosophy

Drivers: **DRY, YAGNI, KISS, scalable minimalism**.

- Ship the smallest system that satisfies the PRD. No speculative modules, services, stores, or pipeline stages.
- Prefer a modular monolith, one repo, one primary datastore (PostgreSQL), HTTPS JSON REST, and GitHub Actions until a named constraint forces otherwise.
- DRY applies to *knowledge and invariants*, not to premature shared libraries. Duplicate once; extract on the third use.
- One reason to change per module. Extend at boundaries; do not abstract for a single caller.
- Every extra box in an ADR needs a PRD-backed reason and a one-line YAGNI veto for the simpler alternative.
- State assumptions. Do not hide tradeoffs. Do not implement the product unless asked.
